;; fib.coll.stack: the `Stack` instances of `Vec` and `List` (stdlib §2.3, §4.5 rows `peek` and `pop`; tranche 2 plan Y5, owner Y5).
;; `peek` and `pop` are the methods of the protocol `Stack` that fib.coll.protocols declares and exports; this part exports no name of its
;; own, it holds the instances (and a private helper). The prelude had no stack, and the tranche 1 part fib.coll.seqs left the instances
;; out on purpose ("peek and pop are tranche 2"). The page's other instances (`SubVec`, `Queue`) wait for their types (tranche 3).
;; Decided here, where the page is silent:
;;  - the end that `conj` adds at is the end that `peek` reads and `pop` removes (Clojure's): the last element of a `Vec`, the first
;;    of a `List`. `peek` of an empty stack is nil, never a trap; `pop` of an empty stack traps `pop: empty`, where Clojure's `pop`
;;    throws (§1.2 P5), and the trap names the function (tranche 1 plan §4.3 rule 8). There is no `try-pop` here.
;;  - `pop` of a `Vec` is the prelude's `vec-pop` (task P1): the tail without its last element, and when the tail holds one the
;;    last leaf of the trie becomes the tail, a new tail array and a new header for a pop and one new path of the trie for 1 pop in 32.
;;  - `pop` of a `List` is its tail, shared, not copied; the tail of a list of one is the empty list.
;; Never `/` on integers; the prelude's `count` and `nth` are not used here (a part calls the prelude's vec-count and vec-nth).
(ns fib.coll.stack (:use fib.core fib.seq fib.coll.protocols fib.coll.seqs))

;; a Vec: the end
(impl (Stack a) (Vec a)
  (peek (self) (let ((n (vec-count self))) (if (> n 0) (some (vec-nth self (- n 1))) nil)))
  (pop (self) (vec-pop self)))

;; a List: the front
(impl (Stack a) (List a)
  (peek (self) (match self ((Cons h _) (some h)) ((Empty) nil)))
  (pop (self) (match self ((Cons _ t) t) ((Empty) (trap "pop: empty")))))
